#10000
"The Place of Repose"
"Four immense slabs of stone form the three walls and roof of this eastward

facing, open-faced structure.  The sheer weight of the stones appears to be

the only thing holding them together, and gaps appear in corners where they

don't fit flushly together.  Fortunately, with such massive weight behind them

it's unlikely anything short of a massive earthquake could move them or cause

them to topple.  The wide opening to the east displays a view of the verdant

greenery spread out before the structure.

"
""
