E
"foliage"
"The foliage consists of a wide variety of shrubbery and flowers.  Some you can

readily identify, such as hawthorne and honeysuckle, and others are exotic and

hard to identify.  They fill the area with a fresh, woodland scent.

"
E
"1 east circle standing 5 stones"
"While you can only see the western edge of the circle of standing stones to

the east, the arc they form certainly give the impression that they would form

a circle.  Most of the stones are broad slabs standing upright and slightly

higher than a tall ent.  A few of the stones are even capped with a stone

crossing over resting on two different standing stones to form a simple

portal.  One such portal provides entrance to the circle of standing stones

due east of here.

"
E
"1 west structure"
"The structure to the west is a large, open-faced building created from four

immense slabs of stone.  One slab forms each of the south, west and north

walls and another caps them to create the roof.  There are no windows or doors

but the entire eastern face of the structure is open, allowing easy entrance.

"
