"1 north 1 west edge Windlass"
"The island of Ent'Moot is roughly circular in shape.  Sheer walls and loose

stone ensure that the cliff face of the island remains unassailable from any

who would attack unless they could somehow fly up the very sides.  Far below,

you can see the rushing waters of the Windlass, the great river that passes

through the Vaasa before eventually making its way down the valley towards

Sos'kul, land of the lizardfolk.

"
E
"greenery garden lush plants"
"There is quite a variety of greenery including plants like germander and

mandrake.  In fact, the plants appear to largely consist of those that a mage

might use in some of their spells.  Although the plants are undoubtedly

healthy, most don't look to be in the stage of readiness that would be

required to make them useful to any spell-caster.

"
