E
"Fountain"
"A broad but simple stone fountain consisting of a rounded stone base with a

sort of pyramid of stone blocks set inside.  The lowest stone is the broadest

of the three in the pyramid and forms a rough-cut cylinder atop which is set

the next, smaller stone and then the smallest stone atop that one.  On each of

the three tiers are carved ancient runes.  Water pours out of an opening in

the top, cascading over the runes on each level before collecting in the

rounded stone base.

"
E
"3 pyramid lowest 5 stones"
"The three stones of the pyramid in the fountain appear to be formed from the

same bedrock stone that forms the base.  They were cut separately, carved with

their runes then placed here atop the base of the fountain.

"
