  if( !char_in_room( ch, find_room( 10003 ) ) )

    end;

  act_tochar( #runes2, ch );

  }

"
E
"rune_intro"
"The runes are an ancient dialect of entish from about as far back as ent

memory runs.  Only one as skilled in the ent language as yourself would have

any chance of decyphering them and even as skilled as you are it takes some

work.

"
E
"ent"
"The runes appear to be largely entish in nature and may even be some older

dialect of entish but you aren't able to understand them.

"
E
"cant_read"
"Whatever the runes are, they're nothing more than symbols carved in stone to

you.  Perhaps they aren't actually anything more than decoration after all.

"
E
"runes1"
"The runes appear to run in a spiral down the fountain and you need to slowly

circle the fountain several times to read them all.

"
E
"rrunes1"
"$n begins to slowly walk about the fountain as $e studies the runes intently.

"
E
"runes2"
"The runes appear to record some of the entish history and values.  So far

you've been able to decipher sections on the following topics: @bhistory@n,

and @bfaith@n.  You can @bread@n the section name to further translate what it

says.

"
