"history"
"@YThe history of the ents is a long one.  A tale largely lost to time and the

ages.  Contained here is what the elders knew when first this fountain was

laid.@n

"
E
"history2"
"@YWe are an old race and some say we come from the same stock as the trolls. 

That in a time of fire and death, ruled by dragons, the trolls chose the dark

caves and dank swamps, hiding in their cowardice and ultimately serving those

that brought the death.

"
E
"history3"
"@YIt is said that we ents chose the path of light, defending the Great Forest

with our very bodies and souls rather than letting it fall before the flame of

death.  In reward for our sacrifice, Cynnis blessed us with the hearty

resilience of the trees themselves.@n

"
E
"history4"
"@YThat is the reason why the trolls are unseemly as a result of their evil

nature and we, as goodly folk, are not althouth we are both of the same

stock.  Why some confuse us for trolls or trolls for us, simply on the

resemblance of our appearance and why we are so very different.  Why trolls

live in dark caves and beneath the ground and why we still live in the woods,

protecting its life.@n

"
E
"no"
"Try as you might, you just can't make out the runes.

"
E
