E
"faith"
"@YMost ents choose to follow in faithful worship of Cynnis.  Although there

are many gods and goddesses in the realms of the heavens, it was Cynnis who

protected us in the time of Fire and Death.@n

"
E
"faith2"
"@YMany rangers and elves also follow the faith and Cynnis is also known as the

Mother of Life and Mother Nature.  What the rest of the races fail to realize,

even the elves most of the time, is that Cynnis is the Vaasa and the Vaasa is

Cynnis.  Cynnis permits the elves to live there and the elves live in harmony

with the land but it is we ents who are the caretakers of the land as Cynnis

has ordained.@n

"
E
"faith3"
"@YShould the Vaasa fall, so should Cynnis fall with it.  That is why we

protect the land even as it protects us.  It is our mother, it is our child,

it is as much our family as we are family to each other.  Wherever an ent

travels, it takes with it the heart of Cynnis, the seed of the land's life and

the hope of renewal.@n

"
