"1 west 1 south edge Windlass"
"The island of Ent'Moot is roughly circular in shape.  Sheer walls and loose

stone ensure that the cliff face of the island remains unassailable from any

who would attack unless they could somehow fly up the very sides.  Far below,

you can see the waters of the Windlass rushing off continuing on its journey

away from Ent'Moot.  The waters continue on their path through the Vaasa

before eventually making their way down the valley towards Sos'kul, land of

the lizardfolk.

"
E
"tree oak"
"The oak tree is ancient and immensely large.  It isn't so large as a shuvana

tree but, for an oak, it puts up a very proud figure of a tree standing much

taller than most oaks ever grow.  The oak flourishes with health but, oddly,

its bole has several hollows very similar to the sort animals would use.

"
E
"4 holes 5 hollows bole"
"The hollows in the bole are much like those an animal might live in but they glimmer with reflected light where items, instead of animals, have been stored in them.

Attempts to reach the items within, however, are foiled by a magic that seems to make the hollows shift and move about the tree whenever anyone other than the person who puts an item in the tree reaches for it.

"
